slug: filestore-first-segment-race
what: Two processes opening a FileStore on the SAME empty directory
  both list it, both see no segments, and both call newSegment(0) with
  CREATE_NEW. One wins; the other dies with
  FileAlreadyExistsException on 00000000000000000000.log. Staggered
  opens are fine, simultaneous ones are not, reproducibly. Found by
  the demo's two-node test, which is the arrangement okay-persist's
  own story describes: a shared log, several processes, one writer.
  Losing that race is NORMAL and the answer is to recover from what
  the winner created, not to throw.
touches: okay-persist/src/main/scala-jvm/okay/persist/FileStore.scala,
  okay-persist/src/test/scala-jvm/okay/persist/...
